+/// Scoreboard that counts texture fetches on Blackwell.
+///
+/// NVIDIA's compiler signals every TEX, TLD and TLD4 of a shader on SB5 and
+/// waits for a result with `DEPBAR.LE SB5, n`, n = the number of fetches
+/// issued after the one whose result is needed; it never gives a fetch its
+/// own scoreboard (GB20x programs compiled by the 615 driver: a 9-tap blur
+/// issues 7 fetches on SB5, then DEPBAR.LE SB5 6, 5, ... 1 before each
+/// accumulation; a shader mixing TEX, TLD, TLD4 and TEX.ULL signals all of
+/// them on SB5 and consumes them the same way).  Texture fetches therefore
+/// complete in issue order, and any number of them can be in flight on one
+/// scoreboard instead of at most the five or six free ones.
+const TEX_COUNTED_SB: u8 = 5;
